<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial size=5&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LTE Uplink TX Verification&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;example workspace&amp;nbsp;demonstrates a fast verification (about 3 seconds) of a CMOS power amplifier with a realistic 2505MHz LTE Uplink Transmit signal as a stimulus.&amp;nbsp; The device-under-test is a&amp;nbsp;Fast Circuit Envelope (FCE) model extracted from GoldenGate.&amp;nbsp; (alternatively, a full co-simulation with GoldenGate could also be used).&amp;nbsp; You will need licenses for the W1719 RF System and W1910 LTE library for the hands-on exercises. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;First, a tour of the measurements.&amp;nbsp; Several simple measurements are presented here, using native SystemVue post-processing capabilities.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;As an optional&amp;nbsp;further step, the Keysight 89600 VSA software and its LTE personality can be used to de-modulate the output of the simulated PA.&amp;nbsp; The 89600 VSA allows more detailed measurements of signal degradation, but does require access to the separate VSA application.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;Model Validation&amp;nbsp;- Measurements &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The spectrum analyzer plot is captured using the &lt;EM&gt;SpectrumAnalyzer&lt;/EM&gt; sink. This is used to quickly assess ACLR and spectral re-growth, for spec pre-compliance.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The &lt;STRONG&gt;CCDF&lt;/STRONG&gt; measurement shows the percentage of time (y-axis) that the instantaneous LTE signal envelope spends above the average power level (x-axis).&amp;nbsp; The &quot;crest factor&quot; of the signal is essentially the dB value of the x-axis intercept, and shows the amplitude of the highest signal peaks normalized to the RMS signal power.&amp;nbsp; A second CCDF trace is a reference trace of white gaussian noise, for comparison.&amp;nbsp;A CCDF curve that abruptly falls to a low value shows lower power handling, or clipping.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The &lt;STRONG&gt;AM-AM and AM-PM&lt;/STRONG&gt; plots show the normalized power gain and output phase of the LTE signal (vs. power level) on a point-by-point basis for the complex-valued modulated carrier envelope.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;When the these traces are flat lines, the DUT is operating in a very linear region.&amp;nbsp; (no change from nominal, regardless of time or amplitude)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;When these traces curve upward or downward vs. power, then DUT is showing some nonlinearity.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;level of simulation modeling is common, and is a considered &quot;Level 1&quot; model.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;When the traces spread into a statistical distribution, then the DUT is&amp;nbsp; demonstrating that some output values depend on the previous signal history in addition to the absolute power levels.&amp;nbsp; These are so-called &quot;baseband memory effects&quot;, which are possible with Level 3 Models.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;This modeling capability is somewhat unique&amp;nbsp;to the GoldenGate FCE modeling process, and also of Keysight&apos;s Circuit Envelope simulation technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;EXERCISES:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;You might want to print this page, or cut &amp;amp; paste it into a word processor document, for easier reading.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Adjust the LTE source power level&lt;/STRONG&gt; using the tuning slider.&amp;nbsp; Change the value&amp;nbsp;from the minimum to the maximum power levels, and note the changes to the output&amp;nbsp;traces.&amp;nbsp; Note the observed power levels and Crest Factors right on the schematic. &lt;EM&gt;(You may need to touch these areas with your mouse to get them to re-read the dataset/EQ&apos;s)&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Change the FCE model file&lt;/STRONG&gt;.&amp;nbsp; Three FCE models for this 2.505 GHz amplifier are provided in the same example directory as this workspace.&amp;nbsp; Double-click on the &lt;EM&gt;FastCircuitEnvelope &lt;/EM&gt;part, and browse to the&amp;nbsp;model file called &quot;&lt;EM&gt;SIM_PA_2p505GHz_m7dBm_level3_ampaccuracy5_freqaccuracy2.fce&lt;/EM&gt;&quot;.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Now re-simulate at the minimum and maximum power levels.&amp;nbsp; What changes do you see in the AM2AM traces?&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;(optional ) Use the 89600 VSA software for deeper post-processing.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;If you have access to the Keysight 89600 VSA software (release 11 or later with its LTE options), activate the VSA measurement sink, and re-simulate.&amp;nbsp; (It takes about 40 seconds the first time it runs).&amp;nbsp; The VSA gives you further measurement ability on the LTE signals, such as&amp;nbsp;EVM for each of the LTE data and control sub-signals; integrated bandwidth power measurements to measure ACLR, and many more capabilities.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;U&gt;User Tip&lt;/U&gt;:&amp;nbsp; After you have simulated into the VSA and observe the results, you can &quot;STOP&quot; the SystemVue simulation, but leave the VSA running; this saves time when you next re-simulate.&amp;nbsp; Slide the slider to a new power level, and this time the VSA continues within about 3 seconds.&amp;nbsp; Explore different FCE models and signal settings.&amp;nbsp; The convenience of this method reduces the amount of time you spend&amp;nbsp;doing verification.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;SUMMARY&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;In this example, the simulations&amp;nbsp;only take a few&amp;nbsp;seconds (about 3sec), yet are fairly realistic modulated PA results.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;This level of verification would be nearly impossible for an analog&amp;nbsp;IC with thousands of transistors using transient Spice and primitive signal sources.&amp;nbsp; A few key capabilities make this easy:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The circuit envelope simulation and model extraction&amp;nbsp;in GoldenGate&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;A&amp;nbsp;fast dataflow simulation backplane in SystemVue, with a full LTE reference library and native&amp;nbsp;FCE model integration; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The SystemVue environment to bridge the&amp;nbsp;design flow gap between&amp;nbsp;Architecture, Implementation, Verification, and Test &amp;amp; Measurement.&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;The exact same tools&amp;nbsp;and signals used here can&amp;nbsp;also be used to generate signals after tape-out to measure the real hardware transceiver with Keysight signal sources and analyzers.&amp;nbsp; This allows you&amp;nbsp;to compare the results directly (&quot;apples to apples&quot;), and to feed back measurements into the architecture process to close your modeling loop.&amp;nbsp; Bring your hardware measurements back into SystemVue, and be using real waveforms for your next design start!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
